In <1993Feb21.213136.16348@gagme.chi.il.us>, Mark G. Rodenkirch writes:
> I'm not sure if this is a bug or not, but this is what happened to me:
> My dog killed a goblin, then stepped onto that square and ate the
> goblin.  The goblin has a dagger and a iron skull cap.  Since my dog
> would step on the square, I assumed that anything else on that square
> could not be cursed.  I was wrong.  The cap was -2 and cursed.  Is
> this a bug or not?

The same sort of thing happened to me on my system (Atari ST).  It's not
a bug, it's a feature...  ;-)

Essentially, if your pet is hungry, it'll go anywhere.  Thus, since it
wanted the Goblin corpse, it was willing to step on the cursed helmet.

The same thing worked in 3.0 for training your pet to walk on cursed
objects.

